    <fr:title text="Topological Space">Topological Space</fr:title>
    <fr:taxon>Definition</fr:taxon>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>
A <html:strong>topological space</html:strong> is a set <fr:tex display="inline">S</fr:tex> together with a collection <fr:tex display="inline">\tau </fr:tex> of subsets called open sets such that
<html:ul><html:li>T1: <fr:tex display="inline">S,\varnothing \in \tau </fr:tex></html:li>
<html:li>T2: <fr:tex display="inline">\forall  U,V\in \tau , U\cap  V\in \tau </fr:tex></html:li>
<html:li>T3: The union of any collection of open sets is open.</html:li></html:ul></html:p>
  </fr:mainmatter>
